(defrule react-loop -> react-loop-exec react-loop-why-split react-loop-init react-loop-phase0 react-loop-phase1 react-loop-phase2 react-loop-phase3-branch react-loop-doom-loop react-loop-why-two-tier react-loop-dispatch react-loop-termination react-loop-design-evolution)
(defrule react-loop-exec -> :nucleus react-loop-exec/n)
(defrule react-loop-exec/n -> :instruction "どの部品が各問い合わせを、どんなループで処理するかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Once a mode is selected, the agent processes each user query through the ReactExecutor, which implements an extended version of the Reason-Act loop [96] (referred to simply as the ReAct loop throughout this paper).")
(defrule react-loop-why-split -> :nucleus react-loop-why-split/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-why-split/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-why-split/a2 :elaboration-additional react-loop-why-split/a3)
(defrule react-loop-why-split/n -> :instruction "標準の方式が考える深さを制限する理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Standard ReAct [96] interleaves reasoning and action in the same turn, which limits deliberation.")
(defrule react-loop-why-split/a1 -> :instruction "道具の定義が考えることに与える圧力を 1 文で書く" :sample "Tool schemas consume context and create pressure to act quickly rather than think deeply.")
(defrule react-loop-why-split/a2 -> :instruction "検討した四つの方式を 1 文で書く" :sample "Four approaches were considered: pure ReAct (simple but biased toward premature action), chain-of-thought prompting (inflexible because it cannot adapt depth to task complexity), a separate thinking phase (enables depth control and prevents premature tool use), and Reflexion-inspired self-critique loops (maximum quality but doubles thinking latency).")
(defrule react-loop-why-split/a3 -> :instruction "採った組み合わせを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev combines the latter two: an explicit thinking phase before action, with optional self-critique for complex tasks.")
(defrule react-loop-init -> :nucleus react-loop-init/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-init/a1)
(defrule react-loop-init/n -> :instruction "問い合わせが来たときに実行部が最初に整えるものを 1 文で書く" :sample "When a query arrives, the executor clears any pending injection queue, creates an interrupt token for cancellation support, wraps the conversation history in a ValidatedMessageList (which enforces correct message alternation), and bundles everything into an IterationContext.")
(defrule react-loop-init/a1 -> :instruction "その入れ物が持つ状態を 1 文で書く" :sample "This context object carries all per-query state: iteration counters, one-shot guard flags (to prevent duplicate signals), and references to shared services such as the tool registry and approval manager.")
(defrule react-loop-phase0 -> :nucleus react-loop-phase0/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase0/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase0/a2)
(defrule react-loop-phase0/n -> :instruction "各繰り返しの冒頭で行う文脈の管理を 1 文で書く" :sample "At the start of each iteration, the executor drains the injection queue and runs the staged compactor.")
(defrule react-loop-phase0/a1 -> :instruction "圧縮の段階の数と、それが段階的に強くなることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The compactor monitors token utilization against the context window and applies five progressively aggressive reduction strategies as pressure rises: warning (70%), observation masking (80%), fast pruning (85%), aggressive masking (90%), and full LLM-based compaction (99%).")
(defrule react-loop-phase0/a2 -> :instruction "安い方法で足りることが多いという性質を 1 文で書く" :sample "Section 2.3.6 details each stage; the key property is that cheaper strategies (masking, pruning) often reclaim sufficient space, avoiding the cost of full LLM summarization.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1 -> :nucleus react-loop-phase1/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase1/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase1/a2 :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase1/a3 :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase1/a4 :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase1/a5)
(defrule react-loop-phase1/n -> :instruction "考える段階で、何を道具なしで呼ぶかを 1 文で書く" :sample "If thinking mode is enabled, the executor calls a separate thinking LLM with a tool-free copy of the conversation.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1/a1 -> :instruction "考えを行動から分ける効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "Separating thinking from action prevents premature tool use: when tools are available, models tend to act quickly rather than think deeply.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1/a2 -> :instruction "深さの水準を 1 文で書く" :sample "Four configurable depth levels (OFF, LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH) let users balance latency against deliberation quality on a per-task basis.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1/a3 -> :instruction "最も深い水準で加わる点検を 1 文で書く" :sample "At the HIGH level, self-critique is automatically included: a critique model evaluates the initial trace, and the thinking model refines its reasoning with the critique as additional input.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1/a4 -> :instruction "点検を別の水準にしていた過去と、統合した理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "An earlier design exposed self-critique as a separate fifth level, but users found the distinction confusing; merging it into HIGH simplified the interface without reducing capability, since users who want deep thinking invariably benefit from critique as well.")
(defrule react-loop-phase1/a5 -> :instruction "考えの結果を次の段階へ渡す方法を 1 文で書く" :sample "The final trace is injected into the conversation as a system reminder, making the reasoning visible to the action model in the next phase.")
(defrule react-loop-phase2 -> :nucleus react-loop-phase2/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase2/a1)
(defrule react-loop-phase2/n -> :instruction "行動の段階で組み立てる入力を 1 文で書く" :sample "The executor assembles the full action prompt: the system prompt (composed by PromptComposer from priority-ordered sections), selected memory bullets from the ACE playbook (Section 2.3.6), all tool schemas, and the conversation history including any injected thinking trace.")
(defrule react-loop-phase2/a1 -> :instruction "報告された数が次の繰り返しで果たす役割を 1 文で書く" :sample "The API’s reported token count is used to calibrate the compactor’s utilization estimates for Phase 0 of the next iteration.")
(defrule react-loop-phase3-branch -> :nucleus react-loop-phase3-branch/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-phase3-branch/a1)
(defrule react-loop-phase3-branch/n -> :instruction "応答に道具の呼び出しがあるかで分岐することを 1 文で書く" :sample "The executor branches based on whether the action model produced tool calls.")
(defrule react-loop-phase3-branch/a1 -> :instruction "道具の呼び出しが無いときの分岐を 1 文で書く" :sample "If no tool calls are present: when the previous tool failed, the executor classifies the error (permission denied, file not found, syntax error, rate limit, etc.) and injects a targeted recovery nudge (Section 2.3.5); when there are incomplete todos, it nudges the agent to continue; otherwise, a text-only response with no error signals task completion, and the loop terminates.")
(defrule react-loop-doom-loop -> :nucleus react-loop-doom-loop/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-doom-loop/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-doom-loop/a2)
(defrule react-loop-doom-loop/n -> :instruction "道具の呼び出しがあるとき最初に行う、繰り返しの検出を 1 文で書く" :sample "If tool calls are present, the executor first performs doom-loop detection with a two-tier escalation: each tool call is fingerprinted as an MD5 hash of the tool name and its arguments, and fingerprints are tracked in a sliding window of the 20 most recent calls.")
(defrule react-loop-doom-loop/a1 -> :instruction "同じ呼び出しが 3 回以上現れたときの最初の対処を 1 文で書く" :sample "If any fingerprint appears 3 or more times, the system injects a [SYSTEM WARNING] message into the conversation (e.g., “ the agent has called read_file with the same arguments 3 times; try a different approach ”) and skips tool execution for that turn.")
(defrule react-loop-doom-loop/a2 -> :instruction "警告の後にも再発したときの次の対処と、利用者の二つの選択ごとの動作を 1 文で書く" :sample "If the same fingerprint recurs after the warning, the system escalates to an approval-based pause via the ApprovalManager, presenting the user with “ Agent is repeating the same action.")
(defrule react-loop-why-two-tier -> :nucleus react-loop-why-two-tier/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-why-two-tier/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-why-two-tier/a2)
(defrule react-loop-why-two-tier/n -> :instruction "二段の対処が警告だけより頑丈な理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "This two-tier approach is more robust than warnings alone: LLMs can ignore injected text, but they cannot bypass a genuine execution halt.")
(defrule react-loop-why-two-tier/a1 -> :instruction "従来の安全装置が粗い理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Pre-existing safeguards (iteration caps, consecutive-read counters) are too coarse: they trigger on any repeated tool type rather than on identical (tool, arguments) pairs, and they activate only after many more iterations.")
(defrule react-loop-why-two-tier/a2 -> :instruction "指紋による検出が捕らえるまでの繰り返し回数を 1 文で書く" :sample "Fingerprint-based detection catches stuck loops within 3 repetitions.")
(defrule react-loop-dispatch -> :nucleus react-loop-dispatch/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-dispatch/a1)
(defrule react-loop-dispatch/n -> :instruction "繰り返しが無いときに実行する戦略を選び、結果をどこへ流すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "When no doom loop is detected, the executor selects an execution strategy (parallel via thread pool for independent calls, sequential for dependent ones), runs the tools through the registry, and records each outcome.")
(defrule react-loop-dispatch/a1 -> :instruction "実行後の記憶の更新の流れを 1 文で書く" :sample "After execution, the results feed into the ACE memory pipeline, where a Reflector analyzes what worked and a Curator updates the playbook with new lessons for future queries.")
(defrule react-loop-termination -> :nucleus react-loop-termination/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-termination/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-termination/a2)
(defrule react-loop-termination/n -> :instruction "ループが終わる経路の数を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "The loop ends through one of four paths: the agent explicitly calls a completion tool with a summary and status (success or failure); the agent produces a text response with no tool calls and no error condition (implicit completion); the error-recovery nudge budget is exhausted (three consecutive failed attempts); or the iteration count reaches a configurable safety limit.")
(defrule react-loop-termination/a1 -> :instruction "未完の仕事が残る場合の対処を 1 文で書く" :sample "If outstanding task items remain when the agent signals completion, the system injects additional nudges to address them before accepting termination to prevent premature completion with incomplete work.")
(defrule react-loop-termination/a2 -> :instruction "どの場合も保存することを 1 文で書く" :sample "In all cases, the final conversation state is persisted to the session store.")
(defrule react-loop-design-evolution -> :nucleus react-loop-design-evolution/n :elaboration-additional react-loop-design-evolution/a1 :elaboration-additional react-loop-design-evolution/a2)
(defrule react-loop-design-evolution/n -> :instruction "最初の実験で試したことと、その問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "Early experiments applied self-critique on every thinking output; this proved too slow for routine operations, motivating selective activation only at the HIGH thinking level.")
(defrule react-loop-design-evolution/a1 -> :instruction "繰り返しの検出を足した経緯を 1 文で書く" :sample "Doom-loop detection was added after observing agents repeatedly calling the same tool with identical arguments (e.g., reading a non-existent file in a loop); existing safeguards based on iteration counts and consecutive-read counters were too coarse to catch this pattern.")
(defrule react-loop-design-evolution/a2 -> :instruction "その他の対策が補った失敗の種類を 1 文で書く" :sample "Staged compaction (Section 2.3.6) and todo-based completion validation (Section 2.3.4) addressed additional failure modes discovered during this phase.")
